xclude fixture paths from llmlint's configured input set\n- Severity with the workaround: low\n- Priority estimate: medium (severity with the workaround low; fires consistently; 1 occurrence; raised one level because it fires consistently)\n\n## Examples\n\nA string or recorded response containing `llmlint-ignore[...]` is scanned the same way as a real comment directive on that line.\n\n## Evidence\n\nVerified on host U-17UN402ICR95C. Draft `drafts:onemessagebus-plan/drafts/20260915T160004Z-directive-parser-reads-llmlint-directives-inside`, run `onemessagebus-plan`, manager-authored: `src/domain/ignore.rs:36-40,81-90` locates the marker textually and does not classify host-language comments or quoted data at basis `6134b6bb80407a92375141e1a6ce974c3157188f`. Manager drafts carry no transcript command.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nRecognise directive markers only inside comments, for file syntaxes llmlint declares support for, and treat files of any other syntax as carrying no directives. Quoted data then never reads as a directive, and path exclusion stays available for opaque fixtures.\n\n### Directive scanner — `llmlint` (`src/domain/ignore.rs`)\n\nThe documented directive contract narrows:\n\n```diff\n-A directive is any line containing `llmlint:` followed by an `ignore*` keyword.\n+A directive is an `llmlint-ignore*` marker inside a comment of a supported syntax\n+(line or block comment, per file extension). A marker in a string, or in a file of\n+an unsupported syntax, is not a directive.\n```\n\n## Owning runs\n\nonemessagebus-plan\n",
